agrees with taskId or contains it in taskIds. Schema binding: primitiveId exists in the current registry. Producer binding: tool maps to an actual producer path and current fingerprint. Commit binding: source-only evidence identifies current HEAD; binary evidence identifies an exact SHA and source commit. Fixture binding: runtime fixtures have current hashes. Negative controls: at least one meaningful mutation; not merely {pass:true}. Privacy: configured canary count is nonzero or the receipt explicitly records privacy as not applicable. Interference: motion and input timing claims require an actual monitor. Cleanup: explicit process/session ownership with zero survivors. Evidence layers: the layer required by the claim is present and non-null. Reference integrity: every referenced path exists and every declared hash matches. No self-reference: a task receipt cannot cite itself, its containing lane receipt, or a wrapper derived solely from itself as independent proof. No copy-green: identical normalized receipts for unrelated tasks require an explicit shared source receipt and task-specific assertions. Normalized duplicate clustering Use a normalization that removes only volatile identity fields: Bashwhile IFS= read -r path; do case "$path" in .artifacts/*.json) hash="$( jq -S ' del( .receiptId, .taskId, .taskIds, .startedAt, .endedAt, .durationMs, .repository.gitCommit, .implementationCommit, .progressNote ) ' "$path" | shasum -a 256 | awk "{print \$1}" )" printf '%s\t%s\n' "$hash" "$path" ;; esac done < "$LANE/inputs/changed-paths.txt" \ | sort > "$LANE/raw/receipt-normalized-hashes.tsv" Any cluster spanning multiple SAFE/WF tasks must be traced to shared independent evidence. A copied 30-line wrapper with only the task ID changed is UNVERIFIED_CLAIM until its referenced producer receipt is validated. Ledger and progress reconciliation Run: Bashgit diff --no-ext-diff --find-renames --function-context main...HEAD -- \ .notes/CONSISTENCY-PROGRESS.md \ .notes/oracle/