future remediation pseudodiffs These are hypotheses to falsify first, not publication-ready findings until checked against the actual tree. PT-001 — Unregistered JSON can satisfy a task or whole program Location: scripts/devtools/consistency.ts::discoverReceipts, verifyTask, verifyAll Failure scenario: place a JSON object with disposition: EVALUABLE_PASS, pass: true, one self-asserted negative control, a self-asserted privacy scan, and closed cleanup under a task directory. Likely wrong output: task passes despite unknown producer, missing primitive, wrong task ID, no transaction, no source commit, and no evidence layer. Severity: Critical. Confidence before local control: High. Future remediation: Diffdiff --git a/scripts/devtools/lib/receipt-schema.ts b/scripts/devtools/lib/receipt-schema.ts +export function validateStoredReceipt( + primitiveId: string, + receipt: JsonObject, +): ReceiptValidationResult { + const core = validateReceipt(primitiveId, receipt); + const errors = [...core.errors, ...envelopeErrors(receipt)]; + const producer = asObject(receipt.producerValidation); + if (producer.valid !== true) errors.push("producerValidation.valid must be true"); + if (producer.registryVersion !== RECEIPT_REGISTRY_VERSION) { + errors.push("receipt registry version is not current"); + } + if (producer.registryFingerprint !== receiptRegistryIdentity().registryFingerprint) { + errors.push("receipt registry fingerprint is not current"); + } + return { + ...core, + valid: errors.length === 0, + disposition: errors.length === 0 ? core.disposition : "INVALID_SCHEMA", + errors, + }; +} diff --git a/scripts/devtools/consistency.ts b/scripts/devtools/consistency.ts -import { validateReceipt, ... } from "./lib/receipt-schema.ts"; +import { + receiptSchema, + validateReceipt, + validateStoredReceipt, + ... +} from "./lib/receipt-schema.ts"; for (const entry of discovery.receipts) { const receipt = entry.receipt; + const primitiveId = String(receipt.primitiveId ?? ""); + if (!receiptSchema(primitiveId)) { + errors.push({ code: "unknown-receipt-primitive", detail: entry.path }); + continue; + } + const stored = validateStoredReceipt(primitiveId, receipt); + if (!stored.valid) { + errors.push({ + code: "invalid-producer-receipt", + detail: { path: entry.path, errors: stored.errors }, + }); + continue; + } + const taskIds = Array.isArray(receipt.taskIds) ? receipt.taskIds : []; + if (receipt.taskId !== taskId && !taskIds.includes(taskId)) { + errors.push({ code: "receipt-task-binding-mismatch", detail: entry.path }); + continue; + } Post-remediation falsifier: both forged controls must become nonzero and name the exact admission error. PT-002 — Schema policies are declarative but not enforced Location: receipt-schema.ts::validateReceipt, buildEnvelope, normalizedCleanup Failure scenarios: required evidence layer absent; declared privacy policy violated; same-transaction and declared-transition treated the same as generic strict identity; omitted cleanup becomes closed: true; omitted recursive scan becomes performed: true. Severity: High. Future remediation: Diff function normalizedCleanup(value: unknown): JsonObject { const cleanup = asObject(value); return { ...cleanup, - closed: typeof cleanup.closed === "boolean" ? cleanup.closed : true, + closed: cleanup.closed === true, + explicit: typeof cleanup.closed === "boolean", survivors: Array.isArray(cleanup.survivors) ? cleanup.survivors : [], }; } if (isEvaluable(requestedDisposition)) { + for (const layer of definition.requiredEvidenceLayers) { + if (asObject(receipt.evidence)[layer] == null) { + errors.push(`missing required evidence layer: ${layer}`); + } + } + + switch (definition.identityPolicy) { + case "none": + break; + case "strict-target": + errors.push(...strictTargetIdentityErrors(receipt)); + break; + case "same-transaction": + errors.push(...sameTransactionIdentityErrors(receipt)); + break; + case "declared-transition": + errors.push(...declaredTransitionIdentityErrors(receipt)); + break; + } + + errors.push(...privacyPolicyErrors(definition.privacyPolicy, receipt)); } - recursiveCanaryScan: { performed: true, matches: [], pass: ... } + recursiveCanaryScan: validatedRecursiveScanFromCandidate(sanitized) Add mutation tests for every policy field, not just report output. PT-003 — Family verification checks declarations, not members Location: consistency.ts::verifyFamily Failure scenario: fixture declares one nonexistent memberReceiptPaths entry. Likely wrong output: EVALUABLE_PASS. Severity: High. Supporting evidence: the bundled unit test explicitly expects this case to pass. attachment-0001-9e90abade0703c0… Future remediation: Diff const members = stringArray(binding.memberReceiptPaths); -memberReceiptCount = members.length; +const validatedMembers = []; +for (const member of members) { + const path = resolveWithin(receiptsRoot, member); + if (!existsSync(path)) { + errors.push({ code: "missing-family-member-receipt", detail: member }); + continue; + } + const parsed = readJson(path); + const primitiveId = String(parsed?.primitiveId ?? ""); + const validation = parsed + ? validateStoredReceipt(primitiveId, parsed) + : null; + if (!validation?.valid || parsed?.disposition !== "EVALUABLE_PASS") { + errors.push({ code: "invalid-family-member-receipt", detail: member }); + continue; + } + validatedMembers.push(member); +} +memberReceiptCount = validatedMembers.length; -} else if (memberReceiptCount === 0) { +} else if ( + members.length === 0 || + validatedMembers.length !== members.length +) { disposition = "BLOCKED_MISSING_PRIMITIVE"; PT-004 — Program governance trusts raw side-channel JSON Location: consistency.ts::verifyAll Failure scenarios: generated-byte-compare.json says byteEqual:true with empty outputHashes; conflicts.json self-asserts the fixed count and empty error arrays; facade-ledger.json self-asserts five booleans. Likely wrong output: governance booleans pass without registered producer, source identity, or independent derivation